  "description": "This autumnal cocktail gets its sweet-tart flavor from a cranberry shrub spiced with black pepper. Its tangy flavor counterbalances a meal's richer flavors, and the shrub is excellent for parties, since it can be prepped in advance.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 8 hr 50 min.\n\nOptional or for serving: Cranberries, for garnish\n\nNotes: For a non-alcoholic alternative, combine 28 g of the cranberry-black pepper shrub, 7 g simple syrup, and 85 g club soda in a wine glass. (Add 2 dashes of orange bitters, if desired—they contain a tiny amount of alcohol.) Garnish with cranberries and serve.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The shrub can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 1 month.",
